# Simple, readable, DRY

When implementing anything in this repo:

- **Keep it simple.** Smallest change that works. No speculative features (timeouts, polling, extra abstractions).
- **Readable over clever.** Clear names, short functions, match neighboring patterns.
- **DRY.** Share logic once (helpers, packages) when the same code would otherwise be copied. Do not invent frameworks.
- **Folder structure.** Put code next to its concern (`connectors/<name>/`, `services/sync/`, page + `api/` on the frontend). Avoid dumping unrelated helpers into giant files when a small shared package/module is clearer.
- **Packages OK.** Use a library when it removes boilerplate; wrap it thinly or not at all.

```text
❌ Copy the same Query/normalize loop into MySQL and Postgres
✅ One sqlutil helper both sources call

❌ Huge page with useMemo/useCallback and unused UX
✅ Straight state + load function matching other pages
```
